    {
      "executionState" : "enabled",
      "id" : "note",
      "kind" : "edit.markdownNote",
      "parameters" : {
        "text" : "# Tiltwood Labyrinth · Generated textures\nA tilting wooden labyrinth: roll a glass marble past the holes and into the brass goal ring. On each Run, five fixed-seed FLUX.2 Klein 4B Distilled jobs generate the maple board, the walnut walls, the felt tray, the swirled glass of the marble, and a study-room panorama that the marble and pearls reflect, each at 1024 × 1024. Asset Cache stores the five images as named slots for this run and previews each one as it becomes ready. The game starts after all five are ready; later frames reuse the bundle without invoking Klein again. Cancel and Run starts a fresh cache and regenerates all five. The model package remains link-only.\n\n**Controls.** Drag the Trackpad crosshair, or drag on the full-screen preview, to tilt the board: the marble rolls toward the crosshair. The centre of the pad holds the board level, and full tilt is reached about a third of the way to each edge. A ring on screen marks the crosshair, and the spirit level at the bottom right shows the current tilt. Action or Space releases the marble at the start of each board and after a lost marble. While the marble rolls, Space hops it over a hole (two hops per board).\n\n**Goal.** Clear five boards: First Roll, Hole Garden, The Maze, The Narrows, and The Gauntlet. A marble that rolls over the middle of a hole drops through, and the rim pulls on a marble that brushes past. Roll over a checkpoint ring to respawn there. Pearls score 100 each. Clearing a board scores 500, ten points for each second under par, 150 for each unused hop, and 300 for a flawless board, and gives back one marble. You start with five marbles; when they run out, press Space to start again.\n\n**Settings.** The game settings JSON sets `tiltSensitivity` (1 normal, 0.25–2.5), `startingMarbles` (1–9), `hopsPerBoard` (0–5), and `firstBoard` (1–5, for practice). Changing a setting restarts the game."
      },
      "resources" : {

      },
      "title" : "How to play"
    },
